From 92c80190e10c4ada0d530c850d185eb0090236f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:03:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] surfaceflinger: composite on the display GPU under PRIME
 offload

Sets MESA_DRM_ROLE=display so Mesa selects drm.gpu.display_vendor_name rather
than the global drm.gpu.vendor_name, which on an offload boot names the
discrete card and drags the compositor onto it along with the apps.

Measured on a muxless laptop (i915 panel, nouveau offload), WebGL Aquarium:
5000 fish with no client composition is 60 fps; 500 fish with client
composition on every frame is 17. The difference is the compositor crossing
PCIe into untiled display-GPU memory, not the application's rendering.

Inert without that property: Mesa falls back to the existing one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NzM9d6UTbgoE8FxzXbB9QK
Change-Id: I90eb7d9b1a0610c28704b79863e47dd1002d67ca
---
 services/surfaceflinger/surfaceflinger.rc | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/surfaceflinger.rc b/services/surfaceflinger/surfaceflinger.rc
index dfdd4aa38c..b34e3420ac 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/surfaceflinger.rc
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/surfaceflinger.rc
@@ -5,3 +5,19 @@ service surfaceflinger /system/bin/surfaceflinger
     capabilities SYS_NICE
     onrestart restart --only-if-running zygote
     task_profiles HighPerformance
+    # Composite on the GPU that owns the display, not on a PRIME offload GPU.
+    #
+    # drm.gpu.vendor_name is global, so on an offload boot it sends every EGL
+    # client to the discrete card -- this one included. On Linux the compositor
+    # stays on the display GPU and only the offloaded app uses the dGPU; doing
+    # it the other way makes SurfaceFlinger read and write display-GPU gralloc
+    # buffers across PCIe, untiled, once per composited frame.
+    #
+    # Measured (muxless laptop, i915 panel + nouveau offload, WebGL Aquarium):
+    # 5000 fish with no client composition is 60 fps; 500 fish with client
+    # composition on every frame is 17.
+    #
+    # Mesa reads drm.gpu.display_vendor_name when this is set, and falls back
+    # to drm.gpu.vendor_name when that property is absent -- so this line is
+    # inert on a single-GPU machine and on any tree without pc_select_egl.sh.
+    setenv MESA_DRM_ROLE display
